Bugfix: Support Multi-Bucket Application Keys in the `b2` backend

Restic failed to open repositories in the Backblaze B2 backend when using
a Multi-Bucket Application Key, including keys restricted to a single
bucket but created through the newer multi-bucket API (for example via
the Backblaze Terraform provider). B2 rejected the authorization request
with the error "This request is not currently supported on API version
number 3".

Restic now uses version 4 of the B2 Native API, which accepts both legacy
and Multi-Bucket Application Keys.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/5741
